          "finding": "Two lower nodes sit at the same level below the gimel foot, with a deep central white separation rising between them. The same-page yagen gimel-tsere has the same paired lower structure and the same attachment to the left foot; the same-page kerega gimel-patah instead has a continuous flat bar across its lower edge. Literal gimel segol has a separate third lower node, and the qamats control has a descending stem. The target preserves the horizontal pair without either lower extension. Certify B5 from the full contour and literal controls, preserving all prior scalars and the unusual preceding lamed B0/BC order.",
